    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12387218/comment/12562846",
          "id": "12562846",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "My bad. I guess this patch should address the problem.\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2008-01-26T11:30:08.094+0000",
          "updated": "2008-01-26T11:30:08.094+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12387218/comment/12562904",
          "id": "12562904",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rolandw",
            "name": "rolandw",
            "key": "rolandw",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Roland Weber",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Hi Oleg,\n\nthat takes care of opening the connection. But it does not address the interval that a thread spends in allocateConnection(). If we want to address that, we'll have to store a thread in the AbortableHttpRequest and interrupt the thread if there is no ConnectionReleaseTrigger. I'm not sure whether that is what we want, but it seems to be a sensible behavior from a user perspective.\n\nPlease go ahead and commit the patch, it already improves the behavior.\n\ncheers,\n  Roland\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rolandw",
            "name": "rolandw",
            "key": "rolandw",
